;; jobs.village.roll (card 5aff1cbf): re-roll an untraded villager's offers by breaking and placing its workstation (lectern at
;; 16 0 16). Live-only facts: whether an AI librarian claims the lectern placed again (day only), loses the profession when it
;; is broken, and whether the trade primitive reads fresh offers each time. Offers do not name an enchantment, so :want is
;; "enchanted_book" (a first-tier librarian may or may not offer one: the roll ends found or no-match after ::max-rolls).
;; A roll breaks only with the villager penned (jobs.lib.villager-pen): rolled cases stand the pen in :blocks (villager cell 16 0 17,
;; a glowstone roof lighting it, the body boxed in its stand 16 0 15; the walled cases close their own cell the same way);
;; jobless villagers are penned by the roll's pen child from carried blocks.
;; A body boxed in its stand cannot see the pen's side walls: the pen cases start
;; beside the pen, look at it from both sides, and are teleported into the stand before the job; roll-librarian-boxed-in-never-seen-pen-walls-digs-out-to-look
;; starts boxed in: the pen child digs the box's entry, walks out to see the walls and shuts the box again.
;; The three sealed-pen cases (sealed-cell, through-the-lectern, sealed-in-dirt) show the body the pen's y+2 cells from inside the villager's cell first: from the stand the roof cells are out of sight, and an unseen cell counts as owed.
;; roll-three-times-in-one-call: three rerolls in one call (no villager offers a netherite ingot), then no-match; the report counts every lectern picked up (yields = uses).
;; Should-succeed: roll-librarian (day, AI villager beside the lectern; needs a pickaxe/axe-free dig: a lectern breaks by hand).
;; roll-villager-walled-in-at-night-is-waited-for-not-gone: a named villager out of sight at night is waited for till day, not :gone.
;; roll-villager-heard-behind-a-wall-by-day-is-walked-toward-not-gone: by day a named villager heard behind a wall is walked toward round it (roll.offers), not :gone.
;; roll-pens-a-jobless-villager-before-it-waits-for-the-job: a jobless NoAI villager 6 blocks off: a jobs.village.pen child (slot :pen) builds the pen and waits; the villager never walks in, so the roll ends with the pen's :not-walked-in.
;; roll-with-no-villager-named-rolls-the-one-that-walked-into-the-pen: the near-end-open pen, a NoAI jobless villager nearer (picked first)
;; and an AI jobless one farther that walks into the pen to the free lectern: the roll rolls that one (roll.villager names it).
;; Should-fail: roll-named-villager-ends-not-walked-in-when-another-walks-into-the-pen (same world, the NoAI one named).
;; roll-with-a-spare-places-it-before-the-pickup-with-a-free-composter-near: with a spare lectern carried, the spare goes in the moment the job is gone and the drop is picked up after (:owed child), so the villager has no time to claim the composter 10 blocks off.
;; Should-fail: a named farmer ends :other-job with no dig; nitwit, absent villager (by day), a villager of another block cell, a cell that stays unseen (ends :cell-unseen, no endless wait).
;; roll-sealed-in-dirt-never-digs-its-way-out-for-the-drop: the body sealed in a pocket under dirt that is another's (a plan footprint stands for the zone), the lectern drop out of reach: the roll ends without breaking the dirt (the pillar escape's roof dig obeys zones).
;; Unseen-cell cases: the body at [8.5 0 16.5] faces west (yaw 90), the lectern is 7 blocks behind it, so it starts unseen; the roll
;; looks first (roll-cell-behind-the-body-is-looked-at); a lectern sealed in obsidian stays unseen (roll-cell-sealed-away-ends-cell-unseen).
